  "title": "Roy T NDE 6346",
  "date": "8-09",
  "content": "At age 55 I had a stress test. My heart was chemically stimulated. After the test, I had chest pain and was afraid of trying to walk for fear of falling. I was taken by wheelchair to the emergency room. I was helped onto a gurney, where I passed out. While unconscious, lying flat on my back, I saw a bright light, or conduit, in the upper right hand corner of the room (the east wall.) The brightly lit conduit or tunnel reminded me of the light that you see above an operating table because of its round shape and its intensity; but this light didn't hurt my eyes. Two angels stood outside of the conduit: one was my younger sister the other a nephew. Both had died in separate car crashes. I didn't visually recognize them, seeing little more than two spheres of white light, but I felt sure of whom they were, and that I was not just guessing. The event seemed to take just an instant, leaving me relaxed and reassured. I was disappointed when I woke up. I was surprised and comforted by the thought that two angels, or spirit-beings, were watching over me. I was disappointed that I woke up before getting the chance to go to the Light.",
